course: dictionary
lesson: 8502
title: Spotting sarcasm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sarcasm is when someone says the opposite of what they mean, in a mocking way, to tease someone or to show they are annoyed. «Oh, great,» she said sarcastically, when it started to rain. Great is a happy word, but it was raining, so she did not mean it was great.
explain: The clues are in the situation and the tone of voice. When the words do not match what is happening, check for sarcasm. «Thanks a LOT» can mean "I'm annoyed with you", especially after someone has done something unkind.
explain: Sarcasm is hard in writing because you cannot hear a voice or see a face. Look for capital letters, a sarcastic word, or a situation that does not fit the words. Ask yourself: does this person really mean what they say?
fact: Sarcastic means saying the opposite of what you mean, in a mocking way.
fact: «Sarcastically» means in a sarcastic way, usually said with a certain tone of voice.
fact: Sarcasm is often used to show you are annoyed, or to make fun of someone.
fact: In texts there is no voice or face, so people sometimes add tags like "/s" or an emoji to show that they are being sarcastic.
fact: A sorry said with a smirk or a sarcastic voice is just another dig, and you are allowed to say so.
exercise: «Oh, great,» she said sarcastically, when it started to rain. What does she really mean? | It is a lovely, sunny day | She is singing a happy song | She wants more rain | *She is annoyed that it is raining
exercise: In «Oh yeah, I've ONLY told you a million times», which word is sarcastic? | *ONLY | told | Oh | you
exercise: A sarcastic «Thanks a LOT» usually means what? | I want to go to a party | I am really grateful for your help | I am very tired | *I am annoyed with you
test: What does sarcastic mean? | *Saying the opposite of what you mean, in a mocking way | Singing loudly with friends | Saying exactly what you mean, very clearly | Speaking very quietly
test: Why is sarcasm hard to spot in texts? | Because texts only use big words | Because texts are always very long | *Because there is no voice or face to show the tone | Because nobody uses texts
exam: «Sorry,» he said with a smirk and rolled his eyes. Is he really sorry? | Yes, he is truly sorry | He is very cold | *No, the smirk shows his sorry is sarcastic, just another dig | He is asking for lunch
